@startuml kg-entity-relationships
title Solvay SPARK Knowledge Graph — Entity–Relationship Map\n732 nodes · 882 edges · 5 entity types · 11 relations

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam defaultFontColor #1F2937
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1F2937
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  FontSize 12
  FontColor #1F2937
}
skinparam legend {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  FontColor #1F2937
}

' Fills are the type colours used in the Knowledge Graph page, lightened so all
' text stays dark on a pale ground; the border carries the full-strength colour.

' --- the fixed, hard-coded vocabulary -------------------------------------
rectangle "<b>stream</b>  (4)\n<size:10>id: stream:<CODE></size>\n<size:10><i>fixed vocabulary — not discovered</i></size>\n--\n<size:10>L2C  Lead to Cash ....... 48</size>\n<size:10>R2R  Record to Report ... 11</size>\n<size:10>I2D  Idea to Delivery .... 9</size>\n<size:10>P2P  Procure to Pay ...... 2</size>" as STREAM #EDE9FE;line:8B5CF6;line.bold

rectangle "<b>system</b>  (6)\n<size:10>id: system:<CODE></size>\n<size:10><i>fixed vocabulary — not discovered</i></size>\n--\n<size:10>S4HANA ..... SAP S/4HANA ... 40</size>\n<size:10>Fiori ...... SAP Fiori ..... 28</size>\n<size:10>ECC ........ SAP ECC ....... 25</size>\n<size:10>eCommerce .. Solvay@eCom ... 10</size>\n<size:10>Salesforce . CRM ............ 4</size>\n<size:10>SOVOS ...... Tax Engine ..... 2</size>" as SYSTEM #E0F2FE;line:0284C7;line.bold

' --- discovered from the corpus -------------------------------------------
rectangle "<b>document</b>  (83)\n<size:10>id: doc:<filename></size>\n<size:10>filename · source · format · chars</size>\n--\n<size:10><i><b>the hub</b> — every stream, system,</i></size>\n<size:10><i>process and spec edge starts here</i></size>" as DOC #F1F5F9;line:64748B;line.bold

rectangle "<b>process</b>  (90)\n<size:10>id: proc:<code></size>\n<size:10>code · in_bpml (79 true / 11 false)</size>\n--\n<size:10>O-030-010  Identify Order</size>\n<size:10>4.5.2.4  Validate Order Readiness</size>" as PROC #DCFCE7;line:10B981;line.bold

rectangle "<b>spec</b>  (549)\n<size:10>id: spec:SPARK-NNNNN</size>\n<size:10>ticket · is_primary</size>\n--\n<size:10>SPARK-22234 · SPARK-21930</size>" as SPEC #FFEDD5;line:F97316;line.bold

DOC -up-> STREAM : <b>belongs_to</b>\n"Belongs to Stream" · 70
DOC -right-> SYSTEM : <b>runs_on</b> "Executes on S/4" · 40\n<b>uses_ui</b> "Fiori Custom App" · 28\n<b>interacts_with</b> "Interacts with ECC" · 25\n<b>connects_to</b> "eCommerce Portal" · 10\n<b>integrates_with</b> "Integrates with CRM" · 4\n<b>interfaces_with</b> "Tax Engine Interface" · 2
DOC -down-> PROC : <b>specifies_process</b>\n"Specifies Process" · 70
DOC -left-> SPEC : <b>implements_ticket</b>\n"Primary Specification" · 13\n<b>references_ticket</b>\n"References Ticket" · 543
PROC -down-> PROC : <b>subprocess_of</b>\n"Subprocess of" · 77\n<i>derived from the BPML workbook</i>

legend bottom
  <b>Reading the map</b>
  Box colours match the node types on the Knowledge Graph page.
  <b>stream</b> and <b>system</b> are a fixed vocabulary, hard-coded in the extractor —
  a platform absent from that list gets no node, however often documents name it.
  Every arrow is directed and starts at a document, except <b>subprocess_of</b>,
  the only relation between two nodes of the same type.
  Ten relations are matched in the document text; <b>subprocess_of</b> alone is derived,
  looked up in BPML_ProcessesHierarchyExtended.xlsx.
  Two systems are connected only through a document naming both — any longer
  route runs via a stream, which is co-membership, not an integration.
end legend

@enduml
